GOAL:
Revision, reinforcement, and strengthening the foundation built during the first 5 days of my Cloud Architect preparation journey.

====================================================
LINUX FUNDAMENTALS REVISION
====================================================

1. Basic File & Directory Commands

Commands:
ls
ls -la
pwd
cd
mkdir
rmdir
touch
cat
cp
mv
rm

Purpose:
Navigation and file management in Linux.


2. File Permissions

Commands:
chmod
chown
ls -l

Purpose:
Managing access control and ownership.

Permission meanings:
r = read
w = write
x = execute

Examples:
chmod 755 script.sh
chmod 644 config.txt
sudo chown sumanth:sumanth script.sh


3. Linux Filesystem Revision

Important directories:

/       Root directory
/home   User files
/etc    Configuration files
/var    Logs and variable data
/tmp    Temporary files
/usr    User programs
/bin    Essential binaries
/opt    Optional software
/dev    Devices
/proc   Process/system info


====================================================
LINUX ADMINISTRATION REVISION
====================================================

4. Process Monitoring

Commands:
ps
ps aux
top
htop
pgrep
kill
kill -9

Examples:
ps aux
top
kill 2345

Purpose:
Monitor and manage running processes.


5. System Monitoring

Commands:
df -h
free -m
hostname
whoami
id
groups

Examples:
df -h
free -m
hostname -I

Purpose:
Monitor system health and identity.


6. Service Management

Commands:
systemctl status nginx
systemctl start nginx
systemctl stop nginx
systemctl restart nginx
systemctl enable nginx

Purpose:
Manage Linux services.


7. Logs & Debugging

Commands:
journalctl
journalctl -u nginx
tail
tail -f

Examples:
journalctl -u nginx
tail -f /var/log/syslog

Purpose:
Debug service/system issues.


